[9.41237, "o", "\u001b[2m- \u001b[0m\u001b[36mread_file\u001b[0m\u001b[2m {\"path\": \"stats.py\"}\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[9.412905, "o", "\u001b[2m- \u001b[0m\u001b[36mread_file\u001b[0m\u001b[2m {\"path\": \"test_stats.py\"}\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[10.598213, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[35m▌ \u001b[0mThe bug is in the implementation: it divides by `len(xs) + 1`.\r\r\n\u001b[2m- \u001b[0m\u001b[36medit_file\u001b[0m\u001b[2m {\"path\": \"stats.py\", \"old_text\": \"    return sum(xs) / (len(\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[10.598468, "o", "\u001b[1;33m┌ permission needed: edit stats.py\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[31m--- a/stats.py\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[32m+++ b/stats.py\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[36m@@ -1,2 +1,2 @@\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[0m def average(xs):\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[31m-    return sum(xs) / (len(xs) + 1)\u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[32m+    return sum(xs) / len(xs)\u001b[0m"]
[10.598474, "o", "\r\r\n\u0001\u001b[1;33m\u0002└ allow? [y]es / [a]lways / [n]o / or type feedback › \u0001\u001b[0m\u0002"]
[14.553704, "o", "y\r\r\n"]
[15.176398, "o", "\u001b[2m- \u001b[0m\u001b[36mrun\u001b[0m\u001b[2m {\"command\": \"python -m unittest test_stats -v\"}\u001b[0m\r\r\n"]
[16.274781, "o", "\r\r\n\u001b[35m▌ \u001b[0mFixed the bug in `stats.py`: `average` computed `sum(xs) / (len(xs) + 1)`; it now divides by `len(xs)`. The test passes (`Ran 1 test ... OK`).\r\r\n\u001b[35m▌ \u001b[0m\r\r\n\u001b[35m▌ \u001b[0mNote: `average([])` will now raise `ZeroDivisionError` — tell me if you want empty input handled.\r\r\n"]
